Expected elements: present

Dense and recognisably the desktop tool. The density problem here is not too much information — it is a middle column with nothing to do next to a pane that is starved.

I re-measured the sibling disagreement; it resolves for surplus, not tightness. Nav column x691–1144 (454px). The tabbed region y63–561 is 499px tall and ink stops at the "By call order. / Self cost" footer (y312–321), leaving 239px empty — 51.5% of the 464px body, close to the 229px on record. Horizontally, Values rows carry a 222px mean label→value dead band (139px at shield_regen_percentage, 309px at `i`) plus a uniform 86px value→type gap: 308px of 436px usable row width, 71%. Surplus in both dimensions. The "tight at 1440" reading is a truncation artifact — depth-4 labels stop at x1061 while the nearest numeric ink is x1121 and the widest number starts x1099, so 38–60px sits dead beyond the ellipsis.

Next door the transaction pane's value column is 168px and breaks 42-char addresses 20/20/2, orphaning "32" (y656–670) and "4c" (y724–738). Columns are 683/454/287 against 913/608/383 — 1.337/1.339/1.335 on a 1.333x ratio: percentage-only, no min-width.

(a) landed; I withdraw the separation complaint here — line 32's arm is 4px cyan against line 29's 2px #919191. (b) inert: "88000 / 200000" already fits; only the unit wraps. (c) confirmed. (d) unchanged, still eating a clause at 2.87:1.

Rating: 6/10

